{
  "slug": "pencil-dev-skill",
  "name": "Pencil Dev Skill",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Teaches AI coding tools to design and edit pencil.dev UI files (.pen format) through the Pencil MCP server. Every read and write goes through the MCP for schema validation. Live screenshots show the design as it looks, and the MCP keeps your changes and the editor in sync while the canvas is open.\n\nRecognises pencil.dev signals automatically: mentions of .pen, .lib.pen, the Pencil canvas, or a design-system folder all activate the skill. Works with Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI, and Cursor. Supports designing screens from scratch, editing existing canvases, instantiating components from .lib.pen libraries, customising design tokens, and bulk-replacing properties across a project.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `pencil-design` (Use this skill for any pencil.dev work, such as designing UI in a .pen file, editing an open…).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install pencil-dev-skill@claude-community` from `Nisus74/pencil-skill`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
